[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Effective memory maintenance includes reviewing and updating stored context so it remains current, accurate, and useful; obsolete or incorrect entries should be edited or removed, while necessary missing context should be added. Backing up existing memories before changes provides a recovery path if an edit accidentally removes context the workflow still requires. Anthropic’s memory guidance recommends regularly reviewing and updating memory as projects evolve.

