[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Decomposition is most valuable when work contains multiple distinct deliverables that require different kinds of content and evaluation. A process map, supporting materials, and a measurement plan are separate outputs, so treating them as coordinated subtasks improves clarity and control.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A defensible vendor evaluation defines the assessment criteria before collecting evidence, then gathers vendor information aligned to those criteria, and finally uses that information to score and rank the vendors.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Campaign ideation should begin with a clear objective and measurable success metrics, plus the target audience and brand voice that constrain relevance, tone, and style. Concept review, finalist selection, approval preparation, launch scheduling, and rollout planning take place after concepts have been generated.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Assessing the audience and consequences establishes the potential impact, while evaluating accuracy, completeness, and unverified claims establishes the output’s quality risk. Those factors can then be measured against organizational escalation criteria before selecting use, iteration, or escalation; recording the decision and rationale provides traceability. Claude outputs can contain factual errors or unsupported claims, so critical and high-stakes information requires validation.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Defining the problem to solve and the applicable constraints establishes the goals, boundaries, and evaluation criteria for subsequent concept generation. Candidate concepts can then be generated, assessed against those constraints, selected, and developed into detailed mock-ups. Anthropic’s prompting guidance recommends clear, explicit instructions and relevant context so Claude can produce targeted results.
